### Issue description

The simplest configuration enabling `khal` results in the following build failure:

```console
       … while calling 'genCalendarStr'

         at /nix/store/6zmjz22khxi92dh43w1dp2mjadysjjy8-source/modules/programs/khal.nix:27:26:

           26|
           27|   genCalendarStr = name: value:
             |                          ^
           28|     concatStringsSep "\n" ([

       error: value is null while a set was expected
```

Here's a minimal config that builds to fail with the latest Home Manager and nixpkgs from nixos-unstable:

```nix
{ ... }:

{
  accounts.calendar.accounts.gvolpe = {
    primary = true;
    khal = {
      enable = true;
      color = "light green";
      glob = "*";
      priority = 10;
      readOnly = false;
      type = "discover";
    };
  };

  programs.khal = {
    enable = true;
    locale = { }; 
  };
}
```

Here's also a PR I made to my personal config, resulting in the same build failure on CI: https://github.com/gvolpe/nix-config/pull/246

Not sure if I'm missing something, but I feel we could do better than failing on a `null` value (e.g. using assertions).

