UnnecessaryEnum REMOVAL

Also figured out part of the typing issues for how I had associated the new types with the existing parsing functions.

Things are more generic!

Helping out with a debugging issue someone had on the Michigan TypeScript (MiTS) Discord, I actually realized that the solution for that one works really well for this scenario too! Glad I helped him work on his issue, it came back as a solution to help fix issues in my own project as well. :)

```ts
// Simple demo
// Rather than using a plain union type, you can make it with a generic union, and base that off a key-value name pair map, which was a pattern I got inspiration from the TS standard library types, it works very well! Makes things easier to use, and it's very smart too.

type Foo<Type extends keyof FooNameMap = keyof FooNameMap> = FooNameMap[Type]

type FooNameMap = {
  a: { type: "a", hi: boolean },
  b: { type: "b", nice: number }
}
```

